  "doc": "Feeds for the CaCl2-consistent anchor (2026-10-11).  Writes feeds.json.  Reads only.\n\nMeasured inputs (GIE ash, 1 N HCl sweep, ICP-OES tables of the bench report):\n  X        = 2.656 eq/kg   multivalent cation eq that dissolve without acid (charge balance, mean of the two\n                           acid-exhausted points 125/150 g/L, gamma-free) -> CaCl2 X/2 mol/kg\n  ENDPOINT = 7.814 mol/kg  acid consumed to the Al onset (125 g/L, 8.00 consumed less the Al already open, P4)\n  ENDPOINT_56 = 7.398      linear interpolation of the sweep to pH 5.6 (sensitivity)\n\nRe-speciation rule (both feeds, dry ash 30,000 kg/h kept):\n  * every metal element total is kept (Ca, Na, K, Mg, Al, Fe, Zn, Pb, Cu, Cr, Ti, S); chloride is ADDED as CaCl2\n    (the assay never measured Cl; the model had Cl only on NaCl/KCl);\n  * the CaCl2 Ca is taken out of Ca(OH)2 (lime-scrubber chemistry: Ca(OH)2 + 2 HCl(g) -> CaCl2 + 2 H2O; raw-ash XRD\n    is calcite-dominated, so the hydroxide is the pool the scrubber consumed);\n  * the mass difference CaCl2 - Ca(OH)2 (+36.89 kg/kmol) is closed with the inert SiO2 filler, the same closure term\n    the 2026-09-09 respeciation used, so dry ash stays 30,000 kg/h and the gate-fee basis is unchanged.\n  NaCl/KCl: model Na and K are kept (element totals).  GIE model Na 55.0 g/kg = leach 54.6 g/kg (0.7 %); model K\n  62.2 g/kg vs leach 53.6 g/kg (+16 %), kept and flagged.\nComposite (canon m5 feed, no measurement): chloride scaled from GIE PER KG OF ASH (X = 2.656 eq/kg, primary);\n  sensitivity = same CaCl2 share of total Ca as GIE (25.4 %, X = 3.60 eq/kg).\nAcid dose: measured endpoint relative to the model's chloride-corrected base inventory,\n  f = ENDPOINT / (B_GIE - X) = 7.814 / 10.566 = 0.740, applied to each feed's own corrected base (B - X).\n  GIE gets exactly 7.814 mol/kg.  The acid-resistant fraction is thereby scaled with the base inventory.\n"
 },
